  2	 * GUI API Route Handlers — Model Registry Domain
  3	 *
  4	 * All REST handlers for the /api/models, /api/model-assignments, and
  5	 * /api/personas endpoints. Follows the domain-split pattern established by
  6	 * `api-repos.ts` — each API domain gets its own handler file imported from
  7	 * `server.ts`.
  8	 *
  9	 * Routes provided:
 10	 *   GET    /api/models                       — list models (auto-init local.json from defaults)
 11	 *   PUT    /api/models                       — bulk-save model list (auto-assign UUIDs)
 12	 *   POST   /api/models/load-defaults         — merge default.json into local.json
 13	 *   GET    /api/model-assignments            — get assignments enriched with stale flag
 14	 *   PUT    /api/model-assignments            — validate + persist assignment data
 15	 *   POST   /api/model-assignments/replace    — swap all occurrences of one model UUID
 16	 *   GET    /api/personas                     — list personas from name-mapping.json
 17	 *   POST   /api/personas/rebuild             — spawn node scripts/build-personas.js
 18	 *
 19	 * Validation rules:
 20	 *   - `PUT /api/models`: auto-assigns UUIDv4 to entries missing `id`; rejects
 21	 *     duplicate slugs and the reserved slug `"inherit"` on non-sentinel entries.
 22	 *   - `PUT /api/models`: returns 409 Conflict when a deletion would leave a
 23	 *     referenced model with no replacement (user must use Replace Model first).
 24	 *   - `PUT /api/model-assignments`: validates all model UUIDs exist in registry
 25	 *     and all persona keys exist in name-mapping.json.
 26	 *   - `POST /api/model-assignments/replace`: rejects same-model swap and
 27	 *     rejects when old_model_id is not currently referenced.
 28	 *
 29	 * Error shape: { error: { code: string, message: string } }
 30	 *   NOT_FOUND        → 404
 31	 *   VALIDATION_ERROR → 400
 32	 *   CONFLICT         → 409
 33	 *   (unhandled)      → 500
 34	 *
 35	 * STDIO discipline: this file never writes to process.stdout.
